        "geology": "Rocky slopes and Loess surface, seasonal streams and ancient agricultural terraces",
        "hydrology": "Rainfall and runoff depended ecosystem. The rocks are runoff source while soil patches are sink for runoff water.",
        "soils": "Are airborne soils results from dust accumulation that form Loess soils.",
        "vegetation": "The typical vegetation in the site are dry warbler scrub land, that rolled by: Haloxylon scoparium in the field, Artemisia sieberi and Zygophyllum dumosum in the slopes. also in the site exists a rich variety of annual vegetation in the winter"
